---
description: >
  Alignment drift after the cold-start install refactor: stale scope path,
  prior aligned stamp, and "init subtree" terminology that hardcodes the
  old module identity.
intent: >
  installMethodologyDocs was stamped aligned under the src/tools/init/
  regime. After the move to src/service/install/ the spec's path is
  stale and the intent's references to "the init subtree" point at a
  subtree that no longer carries that name.
misalignment:
  - spec-gap
---

## Issues

- [ ] `src/service/install/installMethodologyDocs/.aide` frontmatter
  `scope: src/tools/init/installMethodologyDocs`
  Stale path — module moved to
  `src/service/install/installMethodologyDocs/`.
  Traces to: physical move; ancestor `.aide/intent.aide` ->
  outcomes.desired[4] (folder tree as architecture).
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [ ] `src/service/install/installMethodologyDocs/.aide` Context and
  outcomes repeatedly invoke "the init subtree", "every init helper",
  "the init orchestrator"
  Identity drift — the parent spec is no longer the init tool; it is
  the install service. The chokepoint invariant ("every read of `docs/`
  goes through initContent") is unchanged in substance, but the spec
  names the old container.
  Traces to: physical move; ancestor `src/.aide` -> outcomes.desired[2]
  (composition from canonical docs).
  Misalignment: spec-gap

## Retro

Architectural-shift drift: the spec's outcomes are still semantically
correct, but the surface it claims to belong to (the "init subtree") no
longer exists by that name. Folder renames must clear stale `aligned`
stamps; this spec's stamp survived because a code-only refactor doesn't
typically trigger an alignment review.
